{"team":"HOU","col":"#F2405A","identity":"balanced","funnel":"balanced-D","plays_pg":63.0,"adot":8.3,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>Matchup-Driven</h2><p>HOU throw by design. They pass <strong>-0%</strong> over expectation (league -2%) and keep firing even with a lead (43% early-down pass when ahead vs ~41%) \u2014 the kind of pass-first identity that keeps receivers live in every script.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>When they fall behind they abandon the run entirely \u2014 60% pass while trailing, so their pass-catchers have huge comeback-script ceilings.</p><p>They're a heavy under-center team (60% shotgun vs ~68%) \u2014 a pro-style, run-committed structure.</p><p>By the numbers it's a struggling unit \u2014 a 40% success rate (below the 44% average).</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Inside the 20 they lean run-heavy, passing <strong>52%</strong> of the time, funnelling touchdown equity to <strong>Woody Marks</strong>.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 A Balanced Defense</h2><p>They lock down opposing WR2s \u2014 just 30 rec yds/game (vs ~36); fade receiving props there.</p><p>They lock down opposing tight ends \u2014 just 28 rec yds/game (vs ~35); fade receiving props there.</p><p>They surrender <strong>100 rushing</strong> and <strong>210 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). No dominant funnel \u2014 read it matchup by matchup.</p><p>They give up deep shots (22% of throws travel 15+ vs ~19%) \u2014 big-play WR upside against them.</p><p>A stingy, efficient defense \u2014 just 38% success allowed (vs ~44%); temper expectations for opposing skill players.</p><p>They leak <strong>TE touchdowns</strong> (0.34/game vs ~0.24) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: their pass-catchers have massive ceilings in comeback scripts (fade-material as underdogs); <strong>opposing TE anytime-TD</strong> is a repeatable angle.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the cu